## 🛠️ The Sub-3nm Physical Bottleneck
Modern semiconductor design faces a critical physical boundary: **Quantum Tunneling and Thermal Dissipation**. As transistor geometries shrink below 3nm, sub-atomic electron leakage causes spontaneous bit-flips and data corruption. Traditionally, managing this hardware instability requires complex chemical coatings at the foundry level or bloated, high-latency error correction layers (ECC/Exception handling) in software.

Digital Bio Defense absorbs physical hardware instability directly into an unyielding logic plane. Instead of processing heavy, multi-cycle geometric equations, we anchor data integrity to a single-cycle bitwise stencil:

$$EvaluatedState = (InputBitA \land 0x7FFFFFFF) + (InputBitB \land 0x7FFFFFFF)$$

If the payload structure matches this rigid arithmetic rule ($1 + 1 = 2$), it clears the register in a single clock cycle. If an electron leaks or an exploit attempts to corrupt the register state, the hardware-synchronized **Veto Gate** evicts the thread block instantly.

